# The reliability kit this pack runs. Pinned by commit, not vendored.
#
# Vendoring the kit into the pack would put a second copy of ~2,100 lines of
# checker source in every city that installs it, and those copies drift from
# the one being maintained. A pin is the opposite failure mode: it can be out
# of date, and it says so out loud, because `gc <binding> setup` checks out
# this exact commit and every command reports which commit it ran.
#
# To move the pin: change KIT_COMMIT, re-run `gc <binding> setup --force`, and
# record in the pack CHANGELOG what changed in the kit and why it matters here.

KIT_REPO='https://github.com/sjarmak/software-factory-reliability.git'
KIT_COMMIT='d04ce989974e05960e523af400f3b06ff942e2b2'
KIT_COMMIT_SUMMARY='fix(rules): EFFECT-006 names the command that lists the instructed lines'

# NOT YET REACHABLE. `setup` clones KIT_REPO and checks out KIT_COMMIT, and the
# published remote does not carry this commit, so `setup` exits 4 with "the
# remote has no commit" and leaves git metadata and no working tree. That is the
# designed refusal and it is not a workaround away: until the checker commits
# are published, this pack can be read but not run by anyone who does not
# already have the kit. Set FACTORY_KIT_HOME to a checkout you hold to run it.
